{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>לתת</b> — on the pattern of הרה ללת from יללה. The correct form is לתנת ללכת on the pattern of לשבת. Its meaning: they will understand to give prudence to the simple, that they remove foolishness from them; since they cannot attain wisdom and understanding, they will understand their way in this world and how they shall live, as it is stated: the wisdom of the prudent understands his way." "<b>לנער</b> — And to give the youth knowledge through parables. And alef of פתאים stands in place of the yod of פתי, and likewise רפאים. And if the cautious one is wise — he will add learning, and if discerning — he will acquire stratagems, and all this:"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:42.519006770Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}